          "text": "The peak positions index consistently as monoclinic **P2\u2081/c** with \\(Z=4\\). Diagnostic assignments include 110 at 20.71\u00b0, 200 at 22.66\u00b0, \\(11\\bar1\\) at 22.80\u00b0, overlapping 111/\\(20\\bar2\\) near 29.70\u00b0, and 002 at 33.04\u00b0. Refined approximate cell:\n\n\\[\na=8.942\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=5.118\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=6.180\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad\n\\beta=118.76^\\circ .\n\\]\n\nThe lattice and space group are well constrained by the pattern. The light-atom coordinates are less strongly constrained by Cu X-ray powder data, so the CIF below should be regarded as a chemically restrained starting model for final Rietveld refinement rather than a single-crystal-quality determination.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiZnBO3_primary\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder indexing and chemically restrained structure model'\n_audit_creation_date                '2025-01-01'\n\n_chemical_name_common               'Lithium zinc orthoborate'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Li Zn B O3'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'LiZnBO3'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n_chemical_formula_weight            131.13\n\n_cell_length_a                      8.942\n_cell_length_b                      5.118\n_cell_length_c                      6.180\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    118.76\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        247.9\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       3.51\n_diffrn_radiation_probe             x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\n_symmetry_cell_setting              monoclinic\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M      'P 1 21/c 1'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number         14\n\nloop_\n_symmetry_equiv_pos_site_id\n_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x,y+1/2,-z+1/2'\n3  '-x,-y,-z'\n4  'x,-y+1/2,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nZn1 Zn 4 e  0.181  0.120  0.006  1.0  0.010\nLi1 Li 4 e  0.077  0.404  0.636  1.0  0.020\nB1  B  4 e  0.441  0.373  0.299  1.0  0.015\nO1  O  4 e  0.306  0.296  0.307  1.0  0.015\nO2  O  4 e  0.403  0.642  0.335  1.0  0.015\nO3  O  4 e  0.606  0.286  0.450  1.0  0.015\n```\n\nThe metrically equivalent **P2\u2081/n** description is only an alternative setting of the same structure, not a distinct surviving phase. No orthorhombic or trigonal alternative accounts for the characteristic 200/\\(11\\bar1\\) splitting and the monoclinic \\(hl\\) peak sequence as well.",
